{"seq":71,"ts":"2026-10-28T18:01:08.496Z","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","sessionId":"session_4bf32df99f9d47f3b36dcf0c73f9b5ee","causedBy":4,"v":1,"type":"activity.changed","payload":{"activity":"active"}}
{"seq":72,"ts":"2026-10-28T18:01:09.671Z","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","sessionId":"session_4bf32df99f9d47f3b36dcf0c73f9b5ee","v":1,"type":"plan.submitted","payload":{"plan":{"id":"plan_0f2236334c594074aff28f7b3e89ea3e","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","orchestratorSessionId":"session_4bf32df99f9d47f3b36dcf0c73f9b5ee","goal":"Let a customer apply one discount code (SAVE10 or FREESHIP) to a cart, computing the discounted totals in src/cart.ts and rendering a 'Discount (CODE)' line on the receipt in src/receipt.ts.","nodes":[{"id":"cart-discount-pricing","title":"Discount pricing in cart.ts","description":"In src/cart.ts, extend the pricing API so a cart can carry at most one discount code, and own the shared discount contract that the receipt will consume.\n\nChange the signature of `totals` to `totals(cart: Cart, code?: string): Totals` while keeping the no-code call backward compatible (the existing `totals(cart)` must still return the current shape with no discount field).\n\nAdd and export a `Discount` interface and extend `Totals`:\n  export interface Discount { code: string; amount: Cents; }  // code is the normalized UPPERCASE code; amount is negative (the price reduction)\n  export interface Totals { subtotal: Cents; discount?: Discount; shipping: Cents; total: Cents; }\n\nSemantics (codes are case-insensitive — normalize the incoming code with toUpperCase() before matching, and store the normalized form in Discount.code):\n  - subtotal: unchanged, the pre-discount sum.\n  - shipping: computed exactly as today from the PRE-DISCOUNT subtotal against FREE_SHIPPING_THRESHOLD/FLAT_SHIPPING. Do NOT zero shipping for FREESHIP; the waiver is expressed as a discount instead (see invariant below).\n  - SAVE10: amount = -Math.floor(subtotal * 0.1)  (10% off subtotal, rounded DOWN to whole cents).\n  - FREESHIP: amount = -shipping  (negative of the shipping that would otherwise be charged).\n  - Unknown code (after normalization): throw an Error.\n  - The `discount` field is present ONLY when the code actually reduces the price, i.e. amount < 0. So SAVE10 on a $0 subtotal (amount 0) and FREESHIP when shipping is already free (amount 0) both produce no discount field.\n  - Invariant: total = subtotal + shipping + (discount?.amount ?? 0).\n\nAdd tests in src/cart.test.ts covering: SAVE10 rounding down (pick a subtotal where 10% is not a whole cent, e.g. 2999 -> -299), FREESHIP waiving flat shipping under the threshold, FREESHIP producing NO discount field when shipping is already free (at/above threshold and empty cart), an unknown code throwing, and case-insensitivity (e.g. 'save10' behaves like 'SAVE10'). Keep the existing tests passing.\n\nRun `npm run ci` and ensure it passes (prettier format:check, tsc --noEmit, vitest). Keep code prettier-clean.","acceptance":["`totals(cart)` with no code still returns { subtotal, shipping, total } with no discount field and existing cart.test.ts cases pass","`totals` accepts an optional code arg; SAVE10 applies -Math.floor(subtotal*0.1); FREESHIP applies -shipping computed on the pre-discount subtotal","Codes are case-insensitive and Discount.code is stored uppercase; an unknown code throws","The discount field is omitted whenever the code does not reduce the price (amount would be 0), and total === subtotal + shipping + (discount?.amount ?? 0) always holds","New cart.test.ts tests cover SAVE10 rounding, FREESHIP waiver, FREESHIP no-op, unknown-code throw, and case-insensitivity","`npm run ci` passes"],"files":["src/cart.ts","src/cart.test.ts"],"dependsOn":[],"agent":"codex","rationale":"Pricing is the foundational API and owns the shared Discount/Totals contract the receipt depends on."},{"id":"receipt-discount-line","title":"Discount line on the receipt","description":"In src/receipt.ts, surface the discount on the plain-text receipt. This task depends on cart-discount-pricing, which defines and exports the Discount/Totals contract and the `totals(cart, code?)` signature — consume that API, do not re-implement pricing or edit src/cart.ts.\n\nChange the signature to `receipt(cart: Cart, code?: string): string`, keeping the no-code call behaving exactly as today. Pass the code through to `totals(cart, code)`.\n\nWhen the returned totals include a `discount` (present only when the code reduced the price), insert one line BETWEEN the Subtotal line and the Shipping line:\n  - label: `Discount (CODE)` where CODE is the normalized code from `discount.code`.\n  - amount: `formatCents(discount.amount)`, which already renders the negative sign (e.g. '-$2.99').\n  - use the same `line(label, amount)` right-alignment helper and WIDTH as the other rows.\nWhen there is no discount, the output must be byte-for-byte identical to today's receipt.\n\nAdd tests in src/receipt.test.ts covering: a SAVE10 receipt showing the 'Discount (SAVE10)' line with the negative amount in the right place, a FREESHIP receipt showing 'Discount (FREESHIP)', and that passing no code (or a code that does not reduce the price) yields the unchanged receipt. Keep the existing receipt.test.ts cases passing.\n\nRun `npm run ci` and ensure it passes (prettier format:check, tsc --noEmit, vitest). Keep code prettier-clean.","acceptance":["`receipt(cart)` with no code produces byte-for-byte the same output as before","`receipt(cart, code)` passes the code to `totals` and, when a discount applies, prints a `Discount (CODE)` line with the negative amount between Subtotal and Shipping using the existing line/WIDTH alignment","No discount line is printed when the code does not reduce the price","New receipt.test.ts tests cover SAVE10 and FREESHIP discount lines and the unchanged no-discount output","`npm run ci` passes"],"files":["src/receipt.ts","src/receipt.test.ts"],"dependsOn":["cart-discount-pricing"],"agent":"claude-code","rationale":"The receipt is presentation-only and consumes the pricing API, so it must run after the contract is defined and merged."}],"createdAt":"2026-10-28T18:01:09.671Z"}}}
