{"seq":98,"ts":"2026-10-28T18:02:51.402Z","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","sessionId":"session_4bf32df99f9d47f3b36dcf0c73f9b5ee","planNodeId":"receipt-discount-line","v":1,"type":"explain.note","payload":{"text":"Receipt depends on cart (not parallel) so no separate contract task is needed: cart owns and exports the Discount/Totals interface, merges first, and receipt consumes it. File ownership is disjoint (cart.ts/cart.test.ts vs receipt.ts/receipt.test.ts) so there is no write conflict. Receipt is presentation-only; it must not re-implement pricing. Honors the user's split: pricing=codex, receipt=claude-code.","source":"orchestrator"}}
{"seq":99,"ts":"2026-10-28T18:02:51.676Z","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","sessionId":"session_4bf32df99f9d47f3b36dcf0c73f9b5ee","causedBy":4,"v":1,"type":"chat.item","payload":{"item":{"kind":"tool_call","tool":"Bash","inputSummary":"command: helix.cmd explain \"Receipt depends on cart (not parallel) so no separate contract task is needed: cart owns and exports the Discount/Totals interface, merges first, and receipt consumes it. …","outputSummary":"Output received (24 characters)","status":"succeeded"}}}
{"seq":100,"ts":"2026-10-28T18:02:59.020Z","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","sessionId":"session_c947335875c84ce2bc6291b446cd9156","planNodeId":"cart-discount-pricing","causedBy":82,"v":1,"type":"chat.item","payload":{"item":{"kind":"message","role":"assistant","text":"The initial file-read command is taking longer than expected. I’m waiting for it to finish before making changes."}}}
{"seq":101,"ts":"2026-10-28T18:03:00.635Z","projectId":"project_7fcbbd09cc86433ca2350f34cb6cc9af","sessionId":"session_4bf32df99f9d47f3b36dcf0c73f9b5ee","causedBy":4,"v":1,"type":"chat.item","payload":{"item":{"kind":"message","role":"assistant","text":"The plan is submitted and **waiting for your approval in Helix**.\n\n## Plan: Discount codes at checkout — `plan_0f2236334c594074aff28f7b3e89ea3e`\n\n**Two tasks, ordered (receipt depends on pricing):**\n\n1. **`cart-discount-pricing`** — *Codex* · `src/cart.ts`, `src/cart.test.ts`\n   Extends `totals(cart, code?)` and defines/exports the shared `Discount`/`Totals` contract:\n   - SAVE10 → `-Math.floor(subtotal * 0.1)` (rounded down); FREESHIP → `-shipping`; unknown code throws; codes case-insensitive (normalized uppercase).\n   - Shipping threshold still checked on the **pre-discount** subtotal.\n   - `discount` field present **only** when it actually reduces the price, with invariant `total = subtotal + shipping + (discount?.amount ?? 0)`.\n   - No-code `totals(cart)` stays backward-compatible.\n\n2. **`receipt-discount-line`** — *Claude Code* · `src/receipt.ts`, `src/receipt.test.ts` · depends on #1\n   Adds `receipt(cart, code?)`, passes the code through, and renders a `Discount (CODE)` line with the negative amount between Subtotal and Shipping — only when a discount applies. No-code output stays byte-for-byte identical.\n\nBoth tasks carry new tests and are done when `npm run ci` passes.\n\n**Key design choice I locked in:** FREESHIP keeps `shipping` at its normal value and expresses the waiver as a negative discount rather than zeroing shipping — that's precisely what gives the receipt a `Discount (FREESHIP)` line to show. File ownership is disjoint, so the two tasks can't collide; since receipt genuinely consumes the pricing API, I ordered them with `dependsOn` (no separate contract task needed) rather than running in parallel.\n\nApprove it in Helix to kick off the workers — I can't start them myself."}}}
